<Base title="About" description="Why AI Veterinary exists and who is behind it.">
  <article class="wrap narrow hero prose">
    <h1>Why this exists</h1>
    <p>This started in a waiting room. Anyone with several animals spends a lot of time at the vet, and after a while you notice the same thing every visit: the veterinarian examines your animal with real care, and then turns to the computer and types. And types. The consultation report, the discharge note, the letter for the specialist, the email to the owner. Often after hours, often at home.</p>
    <p>AI Veterinary is an attempt to give that time back, and to make good information about animals easier to find for the people who look after them.</p>

    <h2>Two things, one principle</h2>
    <p><strong>For owners:</strong> clear, plain-language information about animal health, reviewed by veterinarians, that helps you understand what is going on and decide when to see a vet.</p>
    <p><strong>For vets:</strong> a documentation assistant that turns a few typed lines into a finished, structured record, with the vet in control of every word.</p>
    <p>The principle behind both: <em>software prepares, a professional decides.</em> Nothing on this site or in our tools replaces a veterinarian's judgement.</p>

    <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
    <p>AI Veterinary is an independent project, built by an animal owner together with practising veterinarians who review the content and test the tools. It is not owned by a practice-software vendor, a pharmaceutical company or a pet-food brand, and it does not sell your data.</p>
    <p>If you are a veterinarian and would like to review articles or try the documentation tool early, <a href="/newsletter">leave your email</a> and say you are a vet. We will get in touch.</p>

    <h2>What we are not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Not a diagnosis service. We will never tell you what your animal has over the internet.</li>
      <li>Not a pharmacy. We explain what medications are for and how to give them, never doses.</li>
      <li>Not a replacement for your vet. When something needs a professional, we say so clearly.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</Base>
